# Load our fork. Always.

This repository is **the97bradley/pipedal**. The live Raspberry Pi (`hostname pipedal`, user `the97bradley`) runs **this fork only**.

## Never stock

- Do **not** leave, restore, serve, overlay-on, or fall back to stock/upstream PiPedal (`rerdavies/pipedal`, Debian package `pipedal` 2.0.111, or any upstream release).
- Do **not** make the UI work against stock `pipedald` (no fake Bluetooth settings, no try/catch that hides missing APIs so stock still “loads”).
- Do **not** treat a Vite overlay on port 5173 as the live UI. Port **80** must be this fork.
- Do **not** copy only the React files onto stock `/etc/pipedal/react` while stock `pipedald` is still the daemon. Overlay onto this fork is fine via `docker/push-pi.sh`.

## Always this fork

After any daemon, Bluetooth, or Settings UI change, **replace stock with this checkout**.

Once this fork is installed, iterate with `docker/push-pi.sh` (scripts + Vite UI, seconds). Do not rebuild the arm64 `.deb` unless `pipedald` / `pipedalconfig` changed. Never overlay onto stock 2.0.111.

If sudo is required on the Pi, give the exact commands. Do not stop at “stock is still installed.”

This project version must be **newer than the installed stock package** so `apt`/`dpkg` replaces it. Never tell anyone to keep 2.0.111.
